===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|:bor|sco:wow|tree=1|id=excitement}}
Attested since the 16th century; borrowed from {{bor|en|sco|wow}}; ultimately a natural exclamation.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/waʊ/}}, {{rhymes|en|aʊ|s=1}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-wow.ogg|a=US}}
* {{a|en|Indic}}
** {{sense|interjection}} {{IPA|en|/ʋɑʋ/}}
** {{sense|noun, verb}} {{IPA|en|/ʋəʋ/}}

====Interjection====
{{en-intj}}

# {{sid|en|astonishment}} {{n-g|An indication of [[excitement]], [[surprise]], [[astonishment]], or [[pleasure]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Wow''', I sure was surprised!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1513|author=w:Gavin Douglas|title=Virgil Æneid (translation) vi. Prol. 19
|passage=Out on thir wanderand spiritis, '''wow!''' thow cryis.}}
# {{n-g|An expression of [[amazement]], [[awe]], or [[admiration]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Wow!''' How do they do that?}}
# {{n-g|Used sarcastically to express disapproval of something.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Wow'''… good job using all of our supplies on the first day.}}

