====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[amaze]] or [[awe]].
#: {{ux|en|He really '''wowed''' the audience.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Joe Sweeney; Mike Yorkey|title=Moving the Needle|year=2015|publisher=John Wiley & Sons|page=200|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=k3AgBQAAQBAJ&pg=PA200&dq=%22wowed%22&hl=&cd=8&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22wowed%22&f=false|isbn=978-1-118-94410-3|passage=If all of us can remember how great it felt to be '''wowed''', why don't we make it a habit to do it more often for others? People remember you when you '''wow''' them, so to differentiate yourself with your clients and customers, think of doing something that would make them remember you.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Nesrine Malik|title=The coronation pulled a screen across a desperate, failing nation – just as intended|date=2023-05-08|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/may/08/coronation-desperate-nation-rotten-system|passage= We have the worst of both worlds: the royal family gives us nothing, and we in turn legitimise it, give it meaning and audience and pay, through subsidies and tax exemptions, for its ability to '''wow''' us.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261019124202/https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/may/08/coronation-desperate-nation-rotten-system|archivedate=19 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|dialect}} To [[wail]]; to [[cry]] mournfully.
## {{lb|en|intransitive|dialect}} Of a cat, to [[mew]].
## {{lb|en|intransitive|dialect}} Of a dog, to [[howl]].

